    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d958">

                <pb facs="1014" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.404/453: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-04T00:00:00+03:00">October 4 [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">6</hi>], 1941—midnight [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >noon</hi>]</date>.<lb/>[Received October 6—2:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1765. Department’s 1112, October 2, 7 p.m., and Embassy’s 1758, October 4, noon.
                    At a conference with representatives of the foreign press on October 4, reported
                    in the Moscow papers, October 5, Lozovski,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d958-f1"/> the
                    Assistant Commissar for Foreign Affairs, read a lengthy prepared statement
                    regarding freedom of worship in the Soviet Union. This statement was
                    unquestionably that promised by Oumansky and mentioned in my telegram under
                    reference. The full text of Lozovski’s prepared statement and of his responses
                    to questions propounded by the newspaper correspondents follows in a telegram
                    bearing the next successive number.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d958-f1" n="34" xml:id="d958-f1-content">
                <p>Solomon Abramovich Lozovsky.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
